The problem with the initial implementation was due to an incorrect loop range in the backward pass, which caused an index error when `j` reached 0. Correcting the loop to ensure `j` doesn't go below 1 fixes this issue.

```python
def cocktail_shaker_sort(arr: List[int]) -> List[int]:
    arr = arr.copy()  # Create a copy to avoid modifying the original list
    n = len(arr)
    for i in range(n - 1):
        # Forward pass
        for j in range(n - i - 1):
            if arr[j] > arr[j + 1]:
                arr[j], arr[j + 1] = arr[j + 1], arr[j]
        # Backward pass
        for j in range(n - i - 2, 0, -1):
            if arr[j] > arr[j - 1]:
                arr[j], arr[j - 1] = arr[j - 1], arr[j]
    return arr
